7.text:
In ${\mathbf R}^{d}$ put $e_{1},\dots ,e_{d}$ for the $d$ orthogonal
segments and write the $d$ non-zero points in the bijective realisation
$X_{i}=t_{i}e_{i}$,
$t_{i}\sim{\rm U}[-1,1]$ i.i.d.  Up to a permutation

${\rm Vol}_{d}({\rm conv}\{0,X_{1},\dots ,X_{d}\})
   =\dfrac{|\det [X_{1}\dots X_{d}]|}{d!}
   =\dfrac{\prod_{i=1}^{d}|t_{i}|}{d!}$,
$|t_{i}|\sim {\rm U}[0,1]$ and $E|t_{i}|=1/2$, so that

\begin{equation*}
E_{d}{\rm Vol}= \frac{1}{d!}\bigl(E|t|\bigr)^{d}
            =\frac{2^{-d}}{d!},\qquad E_{1}{\rm Vol}= \frac12 ,
\end{equation*}
is the ordinary orthogonal simplex.  For $i\ne j$

\begin{equation*}
E\|X_{i}-X_{j}\|
   =E\sqrt{t_{i}^{2}+t_{j}^{2}}
   =\int_{0}^{1}\!\!\int_{0}^{1}\!\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}dxdy
   :=\mu_{2},
\end{equation*}

\begin{equation*}
\mu_{2}
 =\frac{\sqrt2+\log\!\left(1+\sqrt2\right)}{3}
 =\frac{\sqrt2+{\rm arsinh}1}{3}\approx0.7651957 ,
\end{equation*}
and $E\|X_{i}\|=E|t|=1/2$.  On the $N_{d}=d+1$ points
${\cal X}_{d}=\{0,X_{1},\dots ,X_{d}\}$ the mean unordered pair distance
is

\begin{equation*}
\bar D_{d}
 =\frac{dE|t|+\binom d2\mu_{2}}{\binom{d+1}{2}}
 =\frac{1+(d-1)\mu_{2}}{\,d+1\,},\qquad \bar D_{1}=1/2,
\end{equation*}
so that with the origin–inclusive average

\begin{equation*}
R_{d}:=\frac{E_{d}{\rm Vol}}{\bar D_{d}}
     =\frac{d+1}{1+(d-1)\mu_{2}}\;\frac{2^{-d}}{d!},
\qquad R_{1}=1 .
\end{equation*}
In particular

$R_{2}=\dfrac{3}{8\bigl[1+\mu_{2}\bigr]}\approx0.21244$,
$R_{3}=\dfrac{1}{12\bigl[1+2\mu_{2}\bigr]}\approx0.03293$,
$R_{4}= \dfrac{5}{384\bigl[1+3\mu_{2}\bigr]}\approx0.00395$,
$R_{5}\approx3.90\times10^{-4},\dots$

and $R_{d}=O\!\left(2^{-d}d!^{-1}\right)$.  Hence

\[
S_{N}=\sum_{d=1}^{N}R_{d}
     =1+\frac{3}{8(1+\mu_{2})}
      +\frac{1}{12(1+2\mu_{2})}+\cdots
\]

converges essentially after $d=3$.  With
$\mu_{2}=[\sqrt2+\ln(1+\sqrt2)]/3$

\[
S_{\infty}= \sum_{d\ge1}\frac{d+1}{d!\,2^{d}\,[1+(d-1)\mu_{2}]}
          \approx1+0.21244+0.03293+0.00395+0.00039+\cdots
          \approx1.2497,
\]

i.e. $S_{\infty}=1.25$ to the usual three-figure reporting,
$S_{\infty}\approx1.250$, the $d=1$ term being the unity contribution
and the $d\ge2$ tail $0.2497\ldots$.  In the customary
$E{\rm Vol}_{d}/\mu_{2}$ normalisation this is
$\mu_{2}^{-1}\sum_{d\ge1}2^{-d}/d!=(e^{1/2}-1)/\mu_{2}\approx0.848$,
the $1.25$ being the origin-inclusive pair-averaged version quoted in
the thread.  The colliding i.i.d. on the union model gives the
familiar $E{\rm Vol}_{d}=(2d)^{-d}$ and $R_{d}^{c}=(d+1)(2d)^{-d}/
\bigl[1+(d-1)E\|X_{i}-X_{j}\|\bigr]$ with $S^{c}\approx1.11\!-\!1.12$,
about $1.117$, the $1.25$ above being the non-colliding one-point-per-axis
simplex convention. ∎

4.text:
With $R\sim {\rm U}[-1,1]$ put $|R|\sim {\rm U}[0,1]$, $E|R|=1/2$ and

\begin{equation*}
s:=E\sqrt{R_{1}^{2}+R_{2}^{2}}
  =\int_{0}^{1}\!\!\int_{0}^{1}\sqrt{u^{2}+v^{2}}\;du\,dv
  =\frac{\sqrt2+\log (1+\sqrt2)}{3}=0.7651957\ldots ,
\end{equation*}
$E|R_{1}-R_{2}|=2/3$.  Write $X_{i}=R_{i}e_{K_{i}}$,
$K_{i}\sim {\rm Unif}\{1,\dots ,d\}$ i.i.d.  On
$\{K_{1},\dots ,K_{d}\ {\rm distinct}\}$,
${\rm Vol}_{d}{\rm conv}\{0,X_{i}\}=d!^{-1}\prod_{i}|R_{i}|$ and

${\mathbb P}\{K_{1},\dots ,K_{d}\ {\rm distinct}\}=d!/d^{d}$,
so that

\begin{equation*}
E_{d}V:={\mathbb E}{\rm Vol}_{d}
      =\frac{d!}{d^{d}}\frac{(E|R|)^{d}}{d!}
      =\Bigl(\frac1{2d}\Bigr)^{d}=(2d)^{-d},
\qquad E_{1}V=\tfrac12 .
\end{equation*}

For $i\ne j$

\begin{equation*}
E\|X_{i}-X_{j}\|
   =\frac1dE|R_{1}-R_{2}|+\Bigl(1-\frac1d\Bigr)s
   =\frac{\,2/3+(d-1)s\,}{d}=:D_{d},
\end{equation*}
$E\|X_{i}\|=1/2$.  The $d+1$ points $0,X_{1},\dots ,X_{d}$ have
$N_{d}=\binom{d+1}{2}$ unordered pairs, so that the mean unordered pair
distance is

\begin{equation*}
\bar D_{d}
   =\frac{d\frac12+\binom d2D_{d}}{N_{d}}
   =\frac{d+(d-1)\frac23+(d-1)^{2}s}{d(d+1)}
   =\frac{1+\dfrac{2(d-1)}{3d}+\dfrac{(d-1)^{2}}{d}s}{d+1}\; .
\end{equation*}

Hence on the i.i.d. union model

\begin{equation*}
R_{d}:=\frac{E_{d}V}{\bar D_{d}}
     =\frac{d(d+1)(2d)^{-d}}
            {\,d+\dfrac{2(d-1)}3+(d-1)^{2}s\,}
     =\frac{(d+1)(2d)^{-d}}
            {\,1+\dfrac{2(d-1)}{3d}+\dfrac{(d-1)^{2}}{d}s\,},\qquad
     R_{1}=1,
\end{equation*}
and

* $R_{1}=1.00000$,
* $R_{2}=(2\cdot2)^{-2}/\bar D_{2}\approx0.10927$,
* $R_{3}\approx7.51\times10^{-3}$,
* $R_{4}\approx3.79\times10^{-4}$,
* $R_{5}\approx1.51\times10^{-5}$,

$R_{d}=O\!\left((2d)^{-d}\right)$.  The series is essentially exhausted
after $d=3$,

\begin{equation*}
S_{B}=\sum_{d\ge1}R_{d}
     =1+0.10927+0.00751+0.00038+0.000015+\cdots
     \approx1.117\!-\!1.118,
\end{equation*}
i.e. $S_{B}\simeq1.117$ on the three figure scale, $1+R_{2}\approx1.109$
already giving $99\%$ of the non-trivial tail.  With the conventional
point-point normalisation $E_{d}V/D_{d}$ this is
$\sum_{d\ge1}(2d)^{-d}/D_{d}\approx0.844$, the $e^{1/2}-1$ normalisation
being $(e^{1/2}-1)/s\approx0.848$.

Remark.  Imposing the usual one-point-per-axis, i.e. distinct-axis,
convention $X_{i}=R_{i}e_{i}$ one has $E_{d}V=2^{-d}/d!$ and
$\bar D_{d}^{A}=[1+(d-1)s]/(d+1)$.  Then

\begin{equation*}
R_{d}^{A}=\frac{d+1}{d!\,2^{d}\,[1+(d-1)s]},\qquad R_{1}^{A}=1,
\end{equation*}
$R_{2}^{A}\approx0.21244$, $R_{3}^{A}\approx0.03293$, etc., and

\begin{equation*}
S_{A}=\sum_{d\ge1}R_{d}^{A}
     =1+0.21244+0.03293+0.00395+\cdots
     \approx1.2497\approx1.250,
\end{equation*}
the familiar $d!$–normalised origin-inclusive sum, whose
$s$-normalised form is $(e^{1/2}-1)/s\approx0.848$.  This is the
$1.25$ value quoted under the non-colliding, one-point-per-segment
convention. ∎

