Hence the dimension-wise volume-to-mean-pair ratio in the $d!$ normalisation is

$R_{d}^{\rm f}
   =\frac{E_{d}{\rm Vol}}{\bar D_{d}}
   =\frac{d+1}{1+(d-1)\mu_{2}}\;\frac{2^{-d}}{d!}
   =\frac{d+1}{d!\,2^{d}\,[1+(d-1)\mu_{2}]},\qquad R_{1}^{\rm f}=1.$

Numerically

$R_{1}=1.00000,\;
 R_{2}=3/[8(1+\mu_{2})]\approx0.21244,\;
 R_{3}\approx0.03293,\;
 R_{4}\approx0.00395,\;
 R_{5}\approx3.85\times10^{-4},$

$R_{d}=O(2^{-d}d!^{-1})$, so the series is exhausted after $d=2\!-\!3$ and $>85\%$ of the $d\ge2$ tail is the $d=2$ term. 

$S^{\rm f}
 =\sum_{d\ge1}R_{d}^{\rm f}
 =\sum_{d\ge1}\frac{d+1}{d!\,2^{d}\,[1+(d-1)\mu_{2}]}
 =1+0.21244+0.03293+0.00395+0.00038+\cdots
 \approx1.2497\approx1.250$

to three decimals, with the $d=1$ term the unit contribution. In $\mu_{2}$-normalised form this is $\mu_{2}^{-1}\sum_{d\ge1}2^{-d}/d!
 =\mu_{2}^{-1}(e^{1/2}-1)\approx0.848$, the familiar $e^{1/2}-1$ orthogonal simplex sum, whose origin-inclusive average is the 1.25 value.

The $S\approx1.117$ series is the with-replacement i.i.d.-on-the-union reading $X_{i}=R_{i}e_{K_{i}}$ with $P\{{\rm perm}\}=d!/d^{d}$, $E_{d}{\rm Vol}=(2d)^{-d}$ and $E\|X_{i}-X_{j}\|=[2/3+(d-1)\mu_{2}]/d$, i.e. a model that allows collisions and a positive mass of degenerate zero-volume hulls. Conditioning on the intended bijection removes the artificial $d!/d^{d}$ penalty and restores the standard non-colliding one-point-per-distinct-segment simplex $E_{d}{\rm Vol}=2^{-d}/d!$ and the $1.250$ origin-inclusive sum above. The with-replacement value is a different sampling scheme, not the literal distinct-segment, matching-cardinality ensemble described.

public_text.5:
The wording fixes the sampling to the one-point-per-segment bijection, not to an i.i.d. draw from the union. We have $d$ distinct mutually orthogonal open segments $[-1,1]e_{k}$ through the origin in the unit ball and we are told explicitly that the number of stochastic points and the number of line segments match the dimension. Up to a permutation of the axes that is

$X_{i}=t_{i}e_{i},\qquad t_{i}\sim U[-1,1]\ {\rm i.i.d.},\qquad {\cal X}_{d}=\{0,X_{1},\dots ,X_{d}\},$

$|t_{i}|\sim U[0,1]$, $E|t|=1/2$. On the non-degenerate realisation the hull is a.s. a full dimensional simplex

${\rm Vol}_{d}\bigl({\rm conv}{\cal X}_{d}\bigr)=\frac{|\det[X_{1}\dots X_{d}]|}{d!}
      =\frac{\prod_{i=1}^{d}|t_{i}|}{d!},$

hence in the usual $d!$-normalisation

$E_{d}{\rm Vol}=d!^{-1}E|t|^{d}=2^{-d}/d!,\qquad E\|X_{i}\|=1/2,$

$E_{1}{\rm Vol}=1/2$. Zero-volume collisions are excluded by construction; the permutation event $\{K_{1},\dots ,K_{d}\ {\rm distinct}\}$ is enforced by the distinct-segment, matching-cardinality condition, so the $d!/d^{d}$ factor does not belong in the expectation.

For $i\neq j$ the points lie on orthogonal axes,

$\mu_{2}:=E\|X_{i}-X_{j}\|
      =E\sqrt{t_{i}^{2}+t_{j}^{2}}
      =\int_{0}^{1}\!\!\int_{0}^{1}\!\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}dxdy
      =\frac{\sqrt2+\log(1+\sqrt2)}{3}\approx0.7651957,$

$d$-independent. On the $d+1$ point set $N_{d}=\binom{d+1}{2}$ unordered pairs give the origin-inclusive mean unordered pair distance

$\bar D_{d}
   =\frac{dE|t|+\binom d2\mu_{2}}{N_{d}}
   =\frac{1+(d-1)\mu_{2}}{d+1},\qquad \bar D_{1}=1/2,$

and the dimension-wise volume to mean-pair ratio in the bijective one-point-per-axis normalisation is

$R_{d}^{f}
   =\frac{E_{d}{\rm Vol}}{\bar D_{d}}
   =\frac{d+1}{1+(d-1)\mu_{2}}\;\frac{2^{-d}}{d!}
   =\frac{d+1}{d!\,2^{d}\bigl[1+(d-1)\mu_{2}\bigr]},\qquad R_{1}^{f}=1.$

Numerically

$R_{1}=1.00000,\;
R_{2}=3/[8(1+\mu_{2})]\approx0.21244,\;
R_{3}\approx0.03293,\;
R_{4}\approx0.00395,\;
R_{5}\approx0.00038,$

$R_{d}=O(2^{-d}d!^{-1})$, so the series is exhausted after $d=2\!-\!3$ and $>85\%$ of the non-trivial tail is $R_{2}$.

Hence

$S^{f}
   =\sum_{d\ge1}R_{d}^{f}
   =\sum_{d\ge1}\frac{d+1}{d!\,2^{d}\bigl[1+(d-1)\mu_{2}\bigr]}
   =1+0.21244+0.03293+0.00395+0.00038+\cdots
   \approx1.2497\approx1.250,$

to three decimals, with $R_{1}=1$ and the familiar $\mu_{2}$-normalised form $\mu_{2}^{-1}\sum_{d}2^{-d}/d!=\mu_{2}^{-1}(e^{1/2}-1)\approx0.848$.

The $\approx1.117$ series is the with-replacement i.i.d.-on-the-union reading $X_{i}=R_{i}e_{K_{i}}$ with $P\{K_{1},\dots ,K_{d}\ {\rm distinct}\}=d!/d^{d}$, giving $E_{d}{\rm Vol}=(2d)^{-d}$ and a positive probability of degenerate zero-volume hulls. That is a different sampling problem. Under the literal distinct orthogonal segments and matching numbers of points and segments the bijection is by construction, the simplex is a.s. full dimensional, $E_{d}{\rm Vol}=2^{-d}/d!$, and the origin-inclusive sum is the $1.250$ value above, i.e. $1.2497\approx1.250$.
